{ "runner": "anthropic-compatible", "model": "MiniMax-M3", "status": "reviewed", "verdict": "FIX-THEN-SHIP", "findings": "- apps/proxy/src/server.ts: auth gate bypass in remote-prod when cfg.authToken is null — `if (cfg.mode === \"localhost-dev\" && !cfg.authToken) authed = true` only checks mode/dev token; but when mode === \"remote-prod\" with authToken=null, preAuth is false, msg.token check requires cfg.authToken so authed stays false. However `assertDestinationAllowed` still runs and origin is checked, so no full bypass — acceptable. Real issue: `checkAuth` in policy.ts when cfg.mode === \"remote-prod\" with null token returns false correctly, but checkOrigin allows empty origin only in localhost-dev — OK.\n- apps/proxy/src/server.ts: pre-auth via cookie/Authorization is checked but proxy never sets the assmud_session cookie anywhere in the diff; cookie path is dead but harmless. No defect.\n- apps/proxy/src/policy.ts isPrivateOrBlockedIp: missing IPv6 private ranges 2000::/3 isn't blocked (intentional, public), but `100::/64` IPv6 documentation and `::/64` reserved not covered — minor. More importantly, `169.254.169.254` check is done after DNS lookup which is correct order (TOCTOU on DNS rebinding mitigated only if lookup is re-resolved at connect time — diff does not re-resolve before net.connect in bridge.ts, so DNS rebinding between policy check and connect is possible).\n- apps/proxy/src/bridge.ts: `net.connect({ host: opts.host, port: opts.port })` uses the hostname returned from policy but if the caller passed a literal IP via msg.host, isIP branch handled it; however for DNS-resolved hosts the resolved address is used only if host was a name (lookup returns address). Bridge receives `host: dest.address` per server.ts so IP is pinned — OK.\n- apps/proxy/src/server.ts: hello timeout 5s, but message handler uses `ws.once(\"message\")` — if client never sends, connection sits until timeout. Acceptable.\n- apps/proxy/src/policy.ts safeEqual: not truly constant-time relative to token length differences are folded into diff but loop runs to max(len) — OK constant-time-ish.\n- apps/proxy/src/server.ts: in remote-prod with authToken=null, connection is refused — but the `if (cfg.mode === \"localhost-dev\" && !cfg.authToken)` branch should also reject remote-prod with null token; current code falls through to `if (!authed) ws.close(1008, \"unauthorized\")` which is correct.\n- packages/script-engine/src/index.ts: setvar deny-list regex `/cookie|password|token|localStorage|document/i` blocks keys but doesn't block `secret`, `api_key`, `apikey` — incomplete but not a security defect per spec (spec asks no cookie/fetch; those are blocked).\n- packages/script-engine/src/index.ts: trigger regex `new RegExp(t.pattern, t.flags ?? \"\")` can throw ReDoS patterns from user packages — no timeout/regex sanitization. Spec says \"no arbitrary JS, no cookie/fetch\" — ReDoS not explicitly in scope but a hardening gap.\n- packages/profiles/src/index.ts: profiles stored in localStorage including host/port — no secrets required per spec, OK. Token storage `localStorage.setItem(\"assmud_token\", …)` in App.tsx stores auth token in localStorage (XSS-readable) — spec says \"no secrets in repo\" (true, not in repo) but storing tokens in localStorage is a runtime security concern not addressed.\n- packages/terminal/src/buffer.ts: DECSTBM `scrollBottom` when bot < top is clamped to `Math.max(top, bot)` which can produce `top > bot` if params[1] < p(0,1) — actually Math.max ensures top<=bot, OK. But scrollTop=0 default and resize sets scrollTop=0 — OK.\n- packages/terminal/src/buffer.ts: BEL handled, BS handled, CR/LF handled. CUP with `params[0] === 0` defaults to 1 via p(0,1) — correct per ECMA-48.\n- packages/protocol/src/telnet.ts: TTYPE only responds to IS request (payload[0]===1) — OK. MCCP2 DONT, MSSP DONT — OK per plan.\n- apps/web/src/App.tsx: `clientMap.move(dir as \"n\", dir)` passes `nextTitle = dir` so every room title is the direction string, not actual room name — cosmetic, not a defect.\n- apps/web/src/App.tsx: no secrets in repo verified — true.\n- apps/proxy/src/server.ts: origin allowlist with empty origin in remote-prod returns false — OK. checkOrigin missing origin defaults deny in remote-prod — OK.", "raw_log": "/tmp/dispatch-review-log-kUrBnx", "error": null }
